  "script": "Google now pings shoppers the second your product's back in stock. But it only knows what your data tells it. Here are 3 checks so that alert actually goes out. First, compare your warehouse count to your store count today. If the warehouse says 40 and the store says 0, Google shows sold out and the alert never goes out. Second, check how often your stock syncs. Once a night is too slow in peak. Aim for every hour. Third, make sure your price and shipping time match everywhere. 16 in 100 shoppers now start in ChatGPT, and assistants read your data, not your homepage. Keeping all that in sync is what we build at Content Systems.ai. Want us to check your store for free? It's in our bio.",
